cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  TAMA (Rust) is an independent reimplementation of TAMA. It does not replace the
  original method. If you use this software in your research, you MUST cite the
  original TAMA paper (see `preferred-citation` below).
title: TAMA (Rust)
abstract: >-
  A Rust rewrite of TAMA (Transcriptome Annotation by Modular Algorithms), a
  toolkit for processing long-read (Iso-Seq / Nanopore) transcriptome data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Guizard
    given-names: Sébastien
repository-code: https://github.com/sguizard/tama-rs
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    Illuminating the dark side of the human transcriptome with long read
    transcript sequencing
